2026-08-02 (no PR yet -- fill in "PR #N" before merging, per CONTRIBUTING.md) (0 -> 1, 1 more rows): GET_CURRENT_FILE_DATA rows added to grid-jpl.tsv (swe_get_current_file_data coverage, new 2.10.03 entry point). One new case id, GETCURRENTFILEDATA|JPL|0, differs only in the err column's returned file path -- swi_open_jpl_file opens the DE file via swi_fopen(SEI_FILE_PLANET, ...) (swejpl.c:200), so the DE file's own path lands in swed.fidat[0].fnam, and the port's swi_fopen builds that path with DIR_GLUE ('/' on every platform) where the C reference uses Windows' native backslash -- the same documented, deliberate cross-platform path-separator choice already recorded for the five grid-files.tsv GETCURRENTFILEDATA rows in this same change. retc and every hex value column (tfstart/tfend/denum, all 0 per sweph.c:8296's own comment on jpl/star files) match exactly.
